---
import PaletteTable from './PaletteTable.astro';
import { variants } from '../lib/palette';
---
<section class="palette-reference" id="palette" aria-labelledby="palette-title">
  <div class="section-panel">
    <header class="palette-head">
      <h2 id="palette-title">Palette reference</h2>
      <p>All three variants, with Hex, RGB, HSL, and OKLCH side by side.</p>
      <details class="palette-numbering">
        <summary>Colour names and numbering</summary>
        <p>Background colours run from <code>bg0</code> to <code>bg5</code>, and text colours from <code>fg5</code> to <code>fg0</code>. <code>bg0</code> is the darkest background in Coal and Smoulder, and the lightest in Ash. <code>fg0</code> has the most contrast against <code>bg1</code>.</p>
        <p>The examples use <code>bg1</code> for backgrounds and <code>fg1</code> for body text. Any of the <code>fg</code> shades can be used for text.</p>
        <p>CSS names include the variant, like <code>--fl-ash-bg1</code> and <code>--fl-coal-rose</code>. All three palettes are available together. The JSON groups colours by variant and includes their full CSS names.</p>
      </details>
    </header>

{variants.map(variant => <PaletteTable variant={variant} />)}
</div>
</section>
